Subject: [PATCH] webconfig: declare scheduler boolean status functions

The webconfig caller had no declarations for these functions and assumed
an int return. On i386 the per-radio implementation returns bool in AL
while EAX still contains the controller pointer. The caller tests all of
EAX, so a completed radio timer appears permanently active and the North
radio subdoc never gets published. Declare the shared API with the actual
return and argument types, including the related VAP and global checks.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/source/core/wifi_ctrl.h
+++ b/source/core/wifi_ctrl.h
@@ -417,3 +417,10 @@
 void wait_wifi_scan_result(wifi_ctrl_t *ctrl);
+bool check_wifi_csa_sched_timeout_active_status(wifi_ctrl_t *ctrl);
+bool check_wifi_radio_sched_timeout_active_status(wifi_ctrl_t *ctrl);
+bool check_wifi_csa_sched_timeout_active_status_of_radio_index(wifi_ctrl_t *ctrl, int radio_index);
+bool check_wifi_radio_sched_timeout_active_status_of_radio_index(wifi_ctrl_t *ctrl, int radio_index);
+bool check_wifi_vap_sched_timeout_active_status(wifi_ctrl_t *ctrl, BOOL (*callback)(UINT ap_index));
+bool check_wifi_multivap_sched_timeout_active_status(wifi_ctrl_t *ctrl, int radio_index);
+
 bool is_sta_enabled(void);
 void reset_wifi_radios();
